over filled entries (or all k? but only first filled are valid) and increment freq[(unsigned char)entries[i].label]; then find max index. This avoids qsort entirely.\n\nNow implement changes in knn.c and knn.h.\n\nIn knn.h: add struct KNNEntry definition, maybe also declare function prototypes if needed (but we can keep static functions). We'll remove compare_for_sort since no longer used? Actually we might still need it for something else? No. But we should not break other code; removing unused function is fine but must ensure no compilation errors. Since it's defined in knn.h and only used in knn.c, if we don't call it, compiler may warn but okay. We can keep it or remove. Better to remove to avoid dead code.\n\nAlso euclidean_distance_no_sqrt remains same.\n\nNow write new knn.c:\n\n```c\n#include \"knn.h\"\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    // Array of structs for cache-friendly shifts\n    KNNEntry *entries = (KNNEntry *) malloc(sizeof(KNNEntry) * k);\n    if (!entries) exit(1);\n\n    // Initialize with sentinel distances\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        entries[i].dist = -1.0f;\n        entries[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    int filled = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        float *xs = g.xs; // We'll change Group to have xs and ys arrays\n        float *ys = g.ys;\n        char label = g.label;\n        int len = g.length;\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, \n                (Point){xs[j], ys[j]});\n\n            // Binary search insertion point among first filled entries\n            int lo = 0, hi = filled;\n            while (lo < hi) {\n                int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                if (entries[mid].dist <= d)\n                    lo = mid + 1;\n                else\n                    hi = mid;\n            }\n            int pos = lo; // first index where dist > d, or filled 